<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: First-time Visitors vs Automatic Scooter</h1>
<p>Renting a 50cc motorbike in Hanoi costs a flat 200,000 VND per day, but before you sign anything you face one simple decision: a small 50cc bike or a larger automatic scooter. For first-time visitors the choice shapes the whole trip, because it decides how the city feels from the seat. This guide compares the two on speed, weight, control, parking and price, so your first rental matches your plans rather than your nerves. The shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, is open daily from 09:00 to 21:00.</p>
<p>Start with the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub</a> for the full picture of small bikes in the city, then check the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost guide</a> for how prices stack up. Our <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> covers the practical questions visitors ask most, and if you are weighing engine sizes, the comparison of <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/50cc-vs-125cc-hanoi/">50cc and 125cc bikes</a> and the look at <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/scooter-vs-semi-automatic-hanoi/">scooters versus semi-automatics</a> add useful context.</p>
<nav class="toc">
